WEBVTT

00:06.548 --> 00:09.509
[sweet airy music]

00:15.473 --> 00:17.767
♪ Sorry I'm gonna leave ♪

00:17.851 --> 00:19.936
♪ I'm driving so fast ♪

00:20.020 --> 00:22.480
♪ Tell me, why you ♪

00:22.564 --> 00:25.692
♪ Come into me and say ♪

00:25.775 --> 00:28.611
♪ You want me again ♪

00:28.695 --> 00:30.989
♪ Everyone who leaves me ♪

00:32.365 --> 00:35.326
♪ 'Cause I'll be missing you ♪

00:35.410 --> 00:37.829
♪ Together, together ♪

00:42.042 --> 00:44.419
[mellow music]

00:46.171 --> 00:47.464
Can you stay over?

00:50.633 --> 00:54.137
[Yeon-su] This is why…
this is why we had to break up.

00:54.220 --> 00:55.847
NOVEMBER, 2008

00:56.931 --> 00:58.516
Yeon-su, let's grab a bite.

00:58.600 --> 01:01.269
Oh, sorry. I'm not too hungry right now.

01:01.352 --> 01:03.897
Oh, come on. I'll get you banana milk.
Come on.

01:03.980 --> 01:05.482
No, really, I'm fine. It's okay.

01:05.565 --> 01:07.275
- You can go ahead. It's cool.
- Okay.

01:07.358 --> 01:09.360
Yo, Ji-yeon, hurry up.
Let's get a move on.

01:10.445 --> 01:11.529
I'll see you.

01:11.613 --> 01:13.156
[girl] Come on, hurry up!

01:13.239 --> 01:15.700
Not like she'll ever come.
Why bother, right?

01:15.784 --> 01:17.410
[Ji-yeon] Keep it down. She can hear you.

01:17.494 --> 01:18.661
[girl] Why do you care about her so much?

01:18.745 --> 01:20.872
That self-centered princess
doesn't like you.

01:20.955 --> 01:22.540
She doesn't even know you exist.

01:22.624 --> 01:23.917
She's right. Think about it.

01:24.000 --> 01:26.086
Yeon-su's never bothered
treating us or anything.

01:26.169 --> 01:27.420
We always bought her stuff.

01:27.504 --> 01:30.590
Still, it wasn't like she asked us
to buy her any of those things.

01:30.673 --> 01:32.050
It's called being shameless.

01:32.133 --> 01:35.053
She still accepted them
every single time without hesitation.

01:35.136 --> 01:38.014
[girl] Remember the last time?
You always gave her a birthday gift…

01:38.097 --> 01:40.058
[Yeon-su] I absolutely hate being poor.

01:40.642 --> 01:43.812
The worst part is,
I can't be generous or return favors.

01:46.606 --> 01:48.983
Our family's been poor
ever since I was born.

01:49.067 --> 01:50.151
I didn't do it.

01:50.235 --> 01:51.694
I didn't do it either.

01:51.778 --> 01:53.655
[girl] Whatever. It's cool.
Don't worry about it.

01:53.738 --> 01:56.407
[Yeon-su] It made making real friends
or hanging out with them 

01:56.491 --> 01:58.201
uncomfortably difficult.

02:01.704 --> 02:05.250
As a young girl, it was painful.
I'd always be hurting inside.

02:06.835 --> 02:08.336
But I guess it was okay.

02:10.004 --> 02:11.131
Grandma.

02:13.424 --> 02:17.095
You're here again. I told you not to come.
Just go straight home and wait for me.

02:17.178 --> 02:19.597
Are you kidding me?
You want me home alone, all bored?

02:19.681 --> 02:20.723
Good grief.

02:20.807 --> 02:24.185
[Yeon-su] It was okay, I had something
precious that I wanted to protect.

02:24.269 --> 02:26.855
[Ja-gyeong] You hands are freezing.
Have you eaten?

02:26.938 --> 02:28.398
[Yeon-su] Were you extra busy today?

02:28.481 --> 02:29.816
[Ja-gyeong] No, not at all.

02:30.817 --> 02:33.444
- [boy 1] Look at her skirt.
- [boy 2] She's obviously a teacher's pet.

02:33.528 --> 02:35.405
Hey, look at her shoes.
Even my mom wouldn't…

02:35.488 --> 02:37.699
[Yeon-su] That's why I decided
to completely ignore everyone.

02:37.782 --> 02:39.826
Call it being self-centered or whatever.

02:41.035 --> 02:43.079
Simply put, it was more convenient.

02:43.163 --> 02:45.582
[principal] I know a lot of you
are excited for spring.

02:46.166 --> 02:48.418
Despite the weather becoming much cooler,

02:48.501 --> 02:52.130
I would like to thank you all
for being here on this very special day.

02:52.213 --> 02:54.007
Hey. Turn around.

02:54.591 --> 02:55.967
[principal] Seeing all of you here,

02:56.050 --> 02:58.553
I remember standing
in the school field 34 years ago.

02:58.636 --> 03:01.264
[Yeon-su] I was like that all the way,
until I met Choi Ung.

03:01.347 --> 03:02.599
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

03:02.682 --> 03:03.683
I'll kill you…

03:05.560 --> 03:08.605
If you tell anyone
that we're dating, I'll kill you.

03:10.315 --> 03:11.900
And I don't want you bothering me either.

03:11.983 --> 03:14.110
My studies and
getting into university come first.

03:14.944 --> 03:17.572
Likewise, same thing goes for you.
You got that?

03:18.573 --> 03:19.616
Okay.

03:22.285 --> 03:23.369
[sighs]

03:24.579 --> 03:26.247
Is there anything you wanna say to me?

03:27.081 --> 03:29.292
- [rain pattering]
- ["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

03:32.420 --> 03:33.504
Got plans tomorrow?

03:33.588 --> 03:35.924
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

03:40.094 --> 03:41.221
[chuckles softly]

03:42.055 --> 03:44.557
[Yeon-su] The sole person
who helped me close my eyes

03:44.641 --> 03:46.226
and escape from reality,

03:47.310 --> 03:48.228
Choi Ung.

03:52.941 --> 03:54.651
- Did you sleep well?
- Mm-hmm.

03:55.360 --> 03:58.196
- How long did you wait?
- I didn't. I just got here.

04:00.949 --> 04:03.826
[Yeon-su] So they're both symbolic
and represent specific things.

04:04.619 --> 04:06.454
The difference between those two…

04:06.537 --> 04:09.165
"According to this,
the population of the village…"

04:11.251 --> 04:13.753
[groans]
Why am I dozing off?

04:16.798 --> 04:19.092
- "Ever since the 1960s…"
- Mm-hmm.

04:19.926 --> 04:22.679
- "The rapid industrialization of…"
- Uh-huh.

04:23.930 --> 04:25.598
SEO-YEON UNIVERSITY
2012 ADMISSION RESULT

04:25.682 --> 04:27.350
[gentle music]

04:32.313 --> 04:33.606
[Yeon-su laughs happily]

04:34.941 --> 04:36.985
CONGRATULATIONS

04:37.068 --> 04:38.820
NAME: CHOI UNG
MAJOR: ART AND DESIGN

04:50.873 --> 04:51.749
LET'S GO OUTSIDE

04:55.378 --> 04:56.671
[dramatic sigh]

05:12.979 --> 05:14.647
LET'S GO OUTSIDE

05:15.606 --> 05:17.692
[soft gentle music]

05:26.159 --> 05:27.535
- [Ung] Yeon-su.
- [door closes]

05:28.703 --> 05:29.746
What?

05:29.829 --> 05:31.998
- Man, what are you eating?
- Gimbap.

05:32.081 --> 05:34.500
Oh, well. So much for this then.

05:35.168 --> 05:36.127
[chuckles]

05:36.836 --> 05:39.380
Kimchi fried rice, cherry tomatoes.

05:39.464 --> 05:40.631
Did you really make this?

05:40.715 --> 05:43.176
Yeah, of course. Wasn't really that hard.

05:43.259 --> 05:46.721
["Red String of Fate"
by Kim Kyung Hee playing]

05:50.016 --> 05:52.560
- Not so great?
- No, it is.

05:53.895 --> 05:54.979
Exactly.

05:55.063 --> 05:56.689
[Ung chuckles]

05:59.275 --> 06:01.986
- No, I didn't. What are you talking about?
- [rain pattering]

06:04.405 --> 06:05.698
When did I let my guard down?

06:05.782 --> 06:07.492
You were looking all excited
when those girls

06:07.575 --> 06:09.077
were acting really friendly around you.

06:09.160 --> 06:11.245
Tell them to show a little bit of respect.

06:12.330 --> 06:13.831
[Ung] Yeah, yeah, I know.

06:13.915 --> 06:16.626
[Yeon-su] I'm just upset because you were
wasting your time with those kids.

06:16.709 --> 06:17.835
I'm sorry.

06:17.919 --> 06:19.170
[Yeon-su] Oftentimes,

06:20.129 --> 06:22.673
I was yearning for a relief
from the practicality of it all.

06:23.174 --> 06:24.258
COVER LETTER

06:24.342 --> 06:27.053
It gave me
that comforting escape from reality.

06:27.136 --> 06:28.054
[sighs]

06:29.639 --> 06:30.515
Are you done?

06:31.140 --> 06:33.810
Not yet.
I still have a few left to send out.

06:33.893 --> 06:35.228
Do you need it right away?

06:36.145 --> 06:37.396
What do you mean?

06:37.480 --> 06:40.066
I mean, instead of getting a 9-to-5 job,

06:40.149 --> 06:42.568
you can continue to study more
and land a better job in the future.

06:42.652 --> 06:44.779
Except I don't have any time for that.

06:44.862 --> 06:47.782
I need to get a job right now,
gotta become a full-time employee.

06:49.033 --> 06:49.992
You get a job. Then what?

06:53.246 --> 06:56.332
Well, I'm going to save up money so

06:56.874 --> 06:58.626
my grandma won't have to work anymore.

06:59.127 --> 07:00.586
- Is that it?
- What?

07:01.921 --> 07:05.883
I mean, you managed to get scholarships,
while working part-time,

07:05.967 --> 07:08.511
you've been breaking your back
juggling studies and work.

07:08.594 --> 07:11.264
I just thought you'd be aiming
for something a little bigger than that.

07:16.477 --> 07:18.521
[soft music]

07:18.604 --> 07:21.441
[Yeon-su] I wanna live
as well as the average person.

07:21.524 --> 07:23.901
That was my dream for the longest time.

07:26.737 --> 07:28.573
I consider that a success.

07:28.656 --> 07:32.493
Could it be
that maybe this isn't the dream I want?

07:32.577 --> 07:34.620
And you?
What do you plan to do afterwards?

07:35.955 --> 07:37.915
Me? Uhm…

07:37.999 --> 07:40.543
I don't really have a plan.

07:40.626 --> 07:42.753
You're good at drawing
and you enjoy doing it.

07:42.837 --> 07:44.088
You could do that for a living.

07:44.172 --> 07:47.175
[inhales]
I'm going to keep that as a hobby.

07:47.258 --> 07:48.134
[Ung] What I want

07:48.217 --> 07:50.136
is to bask in the sun during the day

07:50.219 --> 07:52.472
and lay underneath a lamp
at night time. That's it.

07:52.555 --> 07:54.307
A stressful life just isn't for me.

07:56.017 --> 07:57.727
[Yeon-su] Perhaps it's destiny.

07:57.810 --> 08:00.188
I was never given a choice to begin with.

08:00.271 --> 08:02.398
[Ung] To be honest,
I'm content with my life.

08:02.482 --> 08:03.774
I got my family and you.

08:03.858 --> 08:06.444
[gentle music]

08:10.406 --> 08:13.910
[Yeon-su] But life often slaps you awake
when you open your eyes.

08:19.499 --> 08:24.003
It's even more cruel,
that ruthless monster called reality.

08:24.086 --> 08:25.129
Why us?

08:26.589 --> 08:29.050
Why do we need to pay the debt instead?

08:30.343 --> 08:32.845
I've never even met…
[inhales shakily]

08:32.929 --> 08:36.516
…this man who's…
who's supposedly my uncle.

08:37.308 --> 08:38.893
[Ja-gyeong] Yeon-su…

08:40.853 --> 08:41.896
Oh, my child.

08:43.773 --> 08:45.233
I really wish that…

08:47.109 --> 08:48.277
[sobbing]

08:48.903 --> 08:51.656
I was only poor enough
to the point that I…

08:52.490 --> 08:54.033
could at least handle it.

08:55.368 --> 08:57.620
[soft somber music]

09:10.550 --> 09:11.592
[driver] We're going now.

09:12.552 --> 09:14.095
[engine starts]

09:17.515 --> 09:20.226
[Yeon-su] Reality sneered
at my false dreams.

09:22.436 --> 09:23.646
Hello, what is it?

09:27.400 --> 09:28.317
[shocked gasp]

09:28.401 --> 09:29.318
[co-worker] Yeon-su, wait!

09:29.860 --> 09:31.237
[Yeon-su] And before I knew it…

09:34.740 --> 09:35.992
[groans]

09:39.620 --> 09:43.040
…just like that,
it was suffocating the life out of me.

09:49.338 --> 09:50.423
[Ung] I'm not gonna go.

09:52.800 --> 09:56.012
[professor] You do realize
this is every student's dream, right?

09:56.095 --> 09:58.598
Do you have any idea
how much talent you have?

09:58.681 --> 10:00.266
I'm sure you've noticed
that you've improved.

10:00.349 --> 10:02.810
And that's only
after being there for six months.

10:02.893 --> 10:05.062
Exactly, that was only six months.

10:05.146 --> 10:07.732
Living there for a few years,
that's a different story.

10:07.815 --> 10:10.401
Being there all by myself
isn't what I want.

10:10.484 --> 10:12.361
Seriously? Is that your reason, huh?

10:12.945 --> 10:15.323
Just think about it,
you can draw all the buildings you love,

10:15.406 --> 10:17.325
and you can push yourself even further.

10:17.408 --> 10:18.576
[sucks teeth]

10:19.160 --> 10:22.038
What's the matter?
Don't you have any ambition?

10:22.121 --> 10:23.998
[chuckles softly]
No. I don't.

10:24.081 --> 10:27.084
I'm not interested in striving
for success or any of that crap.

10:28.085 --> 10:30.546
[Ung] Someone more desperate
deserves that opportunity.

10:30.630 --> 10:32.965
[professor scoffs]
Unbelievable.

10:35.134 --> 10:36.093
[phone buzzing]

10:41.223 --> 10:43.559
SEO-YEON UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
INPATIENT BILL

10:46.896 --> 10:48.773
[somber music]

10:54.487 --> 10:55.529
[door slams]

10:57.073 --> 10:57.907
[door opens]

10:58.699 --> 11:01.535
Oh, wow. When did you get here?

11:02.078 --> 11:04.872
Something's different.
You don't normally wait for me at all.

11:06.040 --> 11:08.042
Are we gonna get lunch? What do you want?

11:08.876 --> 11:10.044
Wanna head out now?

11:12.630 --> 11:13.631
[chuckles softly]

11:14.298 --> 11:16.258
["There For You" by Kim Na Young playing]

11:19.804 --> 11:20.971
[Yeon-su] That's why…

11:22.056 --> 11:24.558
that's the reason
why we couldn't be together…

11:24.642 --> 11:26.977
[Ung] Why do we have to break up?

11:30.523 --> 11:33.442
[Yeon-su] Because our realities
were just way too different.

11:33.526 --> 11:35.444
You always break up with me first.

11:36.987 --> 11:40.825
[Yeon-su] Rather, it was 'cause
my reality was pathetic.

11:40.908 --> 11:43.452
Am I the easiest thing to throw away

11:43.536 --> 11:45.162
among the things you have?

11:48.707 --> 11:49.834
No.

11:52.628 --> 11:54.088
But you're the only one…

11:54.964 --> 11:56.507
that I can get rid of.

11:56.590 --> 11:58.634
["There For You" by Kim Na Young playing]

12:02.054 --> 12:03.431
Why are you doing this?

12:04.223 --> 12:05.724
[Yeon-su] Come to think of it…

12:07.017 --> 12:11.689
maybe it was because
I couldn't even handle my own reality.

12:11.772 --> 12:13.107
[Ung] Give me reason.

12:14.024 --> 12:15.317
[Yeon-su] To be honest…

12:16.569 --> 12:19.196
[Ung] Give me just one reason
why we can't be together.

12:20.614 --> 12:24.118
To be completely honest, I was afraid

12:24.827 --> 12:29.331
someday you'd eventually notice
this inferiority complex of mine.

12:30.166 --> 12:37.006
EPISODE 6
PRIDE AND PREJUDICE

12:37.673 --> 12:40.509
["There For You"
by Kim Na Young continues]

12:48.267 --> 12:49.685
[soft groan]

12:52.730 --> 12:55.566
[Ung] I could have sworn
I was working in my studio.

12:59.862 --> 13:01.030
[groans]

13:06.869 --> 13:07.870
[clunking in distance]

13:17.630 --> 13:19.298
[clunking continues]

13:31.310 --> 13:32.311
[both yelping]

13:32.394 --> 13:34.730
Jeez, you scared me to death!
What the hell!

13:34.813 --> 13:36.524
Don't sneak up on me like that.

13:36.607 --> 13:38.651
- When did you get here?
- Just a while ago.

13:38.734 --> 13:40.903
I thought you'd have trouble
sleeping again. I was worried.

13:42.196 --> 13:44.490
Sleep some more. You didn't get enough.

13:44.573 --> 13:46.408
Hey, what time did I go to bed?

13:46.492 --> 13:48.118
How the hell would I know that?

13:49.036 --> 13:50.079
[groans softly]

13:50.162 --> 13:51.413
[groans, sucks teeth]

13:51.497 --> 13:53.290
How'd I doze off like that?

13:53.374 --> 13:55.584
- I can't believe I slept so well.
- Well, that's good to hear.

13:55.668 --> 13:58.379
Your stopwatch stopped
a bit over 10 p.m. last night.

13:58.462 --> 14:00.589
- Probably around then.
- Maybe.

14:00.673 --> 14:02.925
- Did you take sleeping pills?
- Hmm.

14:03.008 --> 14:04.093
[sighs]

14:04.176 --> 14:06.637
I wondered why you slept
on the sofa instead of your bed.

14:09.974 --> 14:11.392
[Ung] What is that thing?

14:12.309 --> 14:14.311
[soft music]

14:20.109 --> 14:23.362
Bro, you completed 95 hours.

14:23.445 --> 14:25.281
[Eun-ho] Guess you must be
in your element.

14:25.364 --> 14:26.532
You look amazing today.

14:27.074 --> 14:28.826
Hey. What time did you get here again?

14:29.410 --> 14:30.870
Me? Around 7:30 a.m.

14:30.953 --> 14:32.162
Was I alone just then?

14:32.246 --> 14:33.455
- [Eun-ho] Wrong, bro.
- You mean…

14:33.539 --> 14:35.499
I meant not just then.
You've always been alone.

14:35.583 --> 14:36.876
- Oh, screw you.
- [Eun-ho] Oh, that's right.

14:36.959 --> 14:38.711
Ji-ung's gonna be dropping by
some time today,

14:38.794 --> 14:41.130
to edit the footage of you working.
Also, he's gonna be doing

14:41.213 --> 14:43.757
some filming here and there,
specifically the live drawing show.

14:43.841 --> 14:45.509
Let's show him
just how charming you can be.

14:45.593 --> 14:47.344
How awesome you look when you're drawing.

14:47.428 --> 14:49.346
You're no longer the pitiful boy, right?

14:50.264 --> 14:52.224
- [knocks on table]
- Are you listening?

14:53.183 --> 14:55.853
God, how long has it been
since I slept this well?

14:55.936 --> 14:58.147
That good, huh? Didn't wake up at all?

14:58.230 --> 15:00.274
- Mm-hmm.
- Good. That's great.

15:00.357 --> 15:02.610
That's really good.
Means you'll be in great condition.

15:03.861 --> 15:05.362
[sighs]

15:05.446 --> 15:09.033
[Ung] If that's true,
what's this unsettling feeling I have?

15:10.200 --> 15:11.577
[uneasy music]

15:12.328 --> 15:14.914
Honey, it's the weekend,
what are you doing up so early?

15:14.997 --> 15:17.207
That opening ceremony
I've been working so hard on

15:17.291 --> 15:20.920
- these past few weeks is today.
- Oh, really? That's today?

15:21.003 --> 15:23.339
- [Yeon-su] Sit down, grandma.
- Oh, gosh.

15:23.422 --> 15:25.257
Time sure does fly fast.

15:25.341 --> 15:27.635
If you have some time later,
come and visit with grandma Ji-na.

15:27.718 --> 15:30.471
That's okay. I don't want to distract you.

15:30.554 --> 15:33.057
You've worked so hard on that project.

15:33.140 --> 15:35.142
I'm sure you did a fantastic job.

15:35.225 --> 15:37.227
You're the only person in the world
who appreciates me.

15:39.772 --> 15:42.858
Oh, this girl. You know what I heard?
[clears throat]

15:43.651 --> 15:46.862
I heard somewhere that the welfare center,

15:46.946 --> 15:49.782
they're actually accepting
job application forms.

15:49.865 --> 15:51.533
I think I should give it a go.

15:51.617 --> 15:53.452
What? You're kidding me, right?

15:53.535 --> 15:55.537
You must be out of your mind. No way!

15:55.621 --> 15:58.457
Forget it. You're no spring chicken,
I'll tell you that.

15:58.540 --> 16:01.210
I'm bored. That's all.
It's driving me nuts.

16:01.293 --> 16:04.004
I'm stuck in the house all day,
it's sucking the life out of me.

16:04.088 --> 16:05.047
I'm gonna die of suffocation.

16:05.130 --> 16:08.342
There's plenty of stuff for you to do.
Hang out at the senior citizen center--

16:08.425 --> 16:10.678
No, thank you.
There's nothing for me there.

16:10.761 --> 16:12.012
Unless you want me to die of boredom.

16:12.096 --> 16:14.682
Just a bunch of sick, old people
waiting for death.

16:14.765 --> 16:16.558
That's the thing,
you should work on your temper.

16:16.642 --> 16:18.060
- That's why you have no friends.
- [stammers]

16:18.143 --> 16:20.688
What was that? You think
I'm some kind of rabid pit bull?

16:20.771 --> 16:23.107
Anyway, it doesn't matter.
Just thought I'd let you know.

16:23.190 --> 16:26.694
Come on. What if you collapse
in the middle of work?

16:26.777 --> 16:27.653
I can't…

16:29.113 --> 16:33.117
I'm afraid of staying home.
That's what'll ruin me mentally.

16:33.784 --> 16:36.578
What's the disease old people get, huh?

16:36.662 --> 16:37.705
Dementia, that one.

16:39.915 --> 16:42.793
Hey, I'm just being cautious.
I'm not demented yet.

16:42.876 --> 16:45.796
I'm clearheaded
compared to other people my age.

16:45.879 --> 16:49.466
Yeah, no one, I mean no one
can hold a candle to your grandma.

16:50.384 --> 16:52.094
So don't worry about a thing.

16:52.720 --> 16:54.096
Go and eat up.

16:56.015 --> 16:57.808
- Not really worried or anything.
- [clears throat]

16:58.434 --> 17:00.978
Then why are you staring at me
like I'm about to croak?

17:01.061 --> 17:02.312
Not very comforting.

17:02.396 --> 17:05.357
I'm just upset
because it breaks my heart, you know.

17:05.441 --> 17:08.777
You've been working your entire life,
without so much as a vacation.

17:08.861 --> 17:10.446
Can't you just
take it easy once in a while?

17:10.529 --> 17:13.657
What are you talking about?
It doesn't get easier than this.

17:13.741 --> 17:16.577
You cook and prepare my meals
and everything else that I need.

17:16.660 --> 17:18.620
All I do is put my feet up.

17:18.704 --> 17:21.457
Oh, boy, it's so tough. Someone help me.

17:21.540 --> 17:23.083
I'm so exhausted.

17:23.167 --> 17:26.545
[Ja-gyeong] Now, go and eat up.
Enough with this nonsense.

17:28.589 --> 17:29.882
On one condition…

17:31.925 --> 17:33.552
don't do anything demanding.

17:34.678 --> 17:36.764
If you only have to work
for like a few hours a day,

17:36.847 --> 17:38.348
then fine, I'll think about it.

17:38.432 --> 17:41.101
You're acting ridiculous, hmm?

17:42.436 --> 17:46.607
Who do you think you are, young lady?
Do you want me to start calling you mom?

17:46.690 --> 17:49.818
Damn straight.
I'm pretty much your legal guardian.

17:50.486 --> 17:52.821
Better not cross me if you know
what's good for you, young lady.

17:52.905 --> 17:55.157
[chuckles]

17:55.240 --> 17:57.117
You should hear yourself.

17:57.201 --> 17:58.452
- Honey, wait.
- Huh?

17:58.535 --> 17:59.453
- [Chang-sik] Ho.
- Huh?

17:59.536 --> 18:01.914
- What in the world are you wearing?
- Chang-sik, look.

18:01.997 --> 18:03.624
- Not bad. What'd you think?
- This won't do.

18:03.707 --> 18:04.792
Go back and put the other necktie.

18:04.875 --> 18:06.752
The red one
will look better with this suit.

18:06.835 --> 18:08.629
Hi. Have you guys seen
the restaurant owners?

18:08.712 --> 18:10.172
They look like you,
but completely the opposite.

18:10.255 --> 18:12.299
I'm glad you're here. Look at us.

18:12.382 --> 18:14.384
Be honest. How do we look?
Tell us what you think.

18:14.468 --> 18:16.720
Overall, you look like
a couple of Hollywood producers

18:16.804 --> 18:18.764
who live in a wealthy neighborhood.

18:18.847 --> 18:21.433
- I barely recognize you two.
- [both chuckle]

18:21.517 --> 18:23.435
[gasps]
It's for a special occasion.

18:23.519 --> 18:25.562
Ung is going to be
putting on a performance.

18:25.646 --> 18:29.691
That boy's been constantly putting on
a performance 24-7 since he was a kid,

18:29.775 --> 18:31.527
don't know why
you have to get all dressed up for it.

18:31.610 --> 18:34.238
He's not gonna be putting on
some kind of an act, you jackass.

18:34.321 --> 18:36.115
Ung's gonna draw something special

18:36.198 --> 18:38.325
in front of a live audience
and there'll be a huge crowd.

18:38.408 --> 18:40.119
Eun-ho came by last time
and told us about it.

18:40.202 --> 18:41.578
He said we had to come.

18:41.662 --> 18:44.164
To think that our son
never even bothered inviting us.

18:44.248 --> 18:46.583
We still have a lot of time
before it starts, you know.

18:46.667 --> 18:49.002
We need to make sure
to sit at the front row.

18:49.086 --> 18:50.170
Oh, my goodness. Oh, my goodness.

18:50.254 --> 18:52.172
Wait. Honey, we need
to pick up the rice cakes!

18:52.256 --> 18:55.259
I almost forgot! We need to go so we can
pick up and give them the rice cakes.

18:55.342 --> 18:58.637
Wait. Trust me, you oughtta just
hand them out to your neighbors instead,

18:58.720 --> 19:00.055
unless you want him to faint out there.

19:00.139 --> 19:02.432
Still, we need to show
at least some sort of courtesy.

19:02.516 --> 19:04.226
They're going all the way over there

19:04.309 --> 19:05.519
- to watch him draw.
- That's right.

19:05.602 --> 19:08.272
Let me make this clear.
Those people need him more than you think.

19:08.355 --> 19:09.815
They practically begged him to draw.

19:09.898 --> 19:12.442
Everything's all set for him and
he'll pretty much be treated like a king.

19:12.526 --> 19:15.154
My goodness. Is that true?
[excited squeal]

19:16.029 --> 19:17.823
My gosh!

19:17.906 --> 19:19.324
Did you hear that, you fool, huh?

19:19.408 --> 19:22.369
They begged my son to draw for them.
He's important to all those people.

19:22.452 --> 19:24.371
Wait, that's why
he's drawing for them right?

19:24.454 --> 19:26.498
Yep, that's how popular
and competent he is.

19:26.582 --> 19:28.041
[delighted chuckles]

19:28.125 --> 19:31.545
Anyway, you don't have to rush over there.
So just take your time, don't worry.

19:32.671 --> 19:34.298
[guests chatting]

19:35.549 --> 19:38.051
[bright music]

19:40.470 --> 19:41.763
[sighs]
We're at the tail-end

19:41.847 --> 19:42.973
of this long-term project.

19:43.056 --> 19:44.308
D-day is finally here, guys.

19:44.391 --> 19:46.185
- [snaps fingers]
- Oh, that's right.

19:46.268 --> 19:48.228
We should go and grab something to eat

19:48.312 --> 19:51.064
before the others arrive at least.
That's how I believe we'll get through--

19:51.148 --> 19:52.733
- Good idea, except there's no time.
- He's right.

19:52.816 --> 19:54.735
Today is gonna be quite a hectic day.

19:54.818 --> 19:56.820
Why don't we conduct
our final meeting for this over lunch?

19:56.904 --> 19:58.697
I'll call and make the order right now.

19:58.780 --> 20:01.366
No, let me. You all good with sandwiches?

20:01.450 --> 20:02.534
- Yes.
- Hell yeah.

20:03.911 --> 20:05.162
- Oh…
- [quirky music]

20:05.245 --> 20:08.498
Should… should I just get
the same thing for all of us?

20:08.582 --> 20:10.083
Actually, I'm on a diet.

20:10.167 --> 20:13.003
I'll have wheat bread, roast chicken,
olive oil, and pepper, please.

20:13.086 --> 20:14.963
I'd like the steak and cheese sub.
No pickles for me.

20:15.047 --> 20:16.965
- I can't ever eat pickles.
- And for me…

20:17.049 --> 20:19.468
What was that sauce we had
from the last time we ate?

20:19.551 --> 20:20.761
I wrote it down somewhere.

20:22.262 --> 20:24.514
All right, why don't you
let me do it instead?

20:24.598 --> 20:26.892
You'll have what you normally have, right?

20:26.975 --> 20:28.018
Sure.

20:28.101 --> 20:31.355
[quirky music fades]

20:34.191 --> 20:35.317
[yawns]

20:37.027 --> 20:39.488
Ms. Kook, are you doing okay?
You've been looking quite exhausted.

20:39.571 --> 20:41.114
[exhales]
I'm all right.

20:41.823 --> 20:43.200
[Ye-in] Like you asked us to do,

20:43.283 --> 20:44.868
we've organized two
separate press conferences

20:44.952 --> 20:46.203
for Nu-a and Go-oh later.

20:46.787 --> 20:48.747
We've estimated that Jean Ferrat
should be arriving

20:48.830 --> 20:50.332
around the time the drawing show ends.

20:50.415 --> 20:52.501
- He'll come straight from the airport.
- Okay. Thank you very much.

20:53.919 --> 20:56.797
Do you know what time
Go-oh will arrive here? Just an estimate?

20:58.548 --> 20:59.883
[Ung] Wanna sleep over?

21:00.592 --> 21:02.678
[soft music]

21:15.607 --> 21:16.900
[Ye-in] Uhm, Ms. Kook?

21:18.110 --> 21:20.862
- Right. Don't worry. I'll ask him.
- Thanks.

21:20.946 --> 21:21.905
[phone buzzing]

21:21.989 --> 21:25.409
Oh, also, it looks like
Mr. Jang just arrived on the first floor.

21:25.492 --> 21:26.368
I see.

21:27.369 --> 21:28.328
Shouldn't you go greet him?

21:28.412 --> 21:29.913
I'll see him once this thing starts.

21:31.707 --> 21:34.626
Enjoy your meal, guys. We'll meet
at the front door in exactly 30 minutes.

21:34.710 --> 21:36.795
Gotta make some last-minute checks
on the second floor.

21:36.878 --> 21:37.838
- Okay. You got it.
- Understood.

21:40.299 --> 21:42.342
[Ji-ung] Today's interview is gonna be
about you as an artist.

21:42.426 --> 21:45.554
Your creative process. Feel free
to talk about your occupation and such.

21:45.637 --> 21:46.930
What do you mean? Like what?

21:47.014 --> 21:49.141
Like your thoughts
that are embedded in your work,

21:49.224 --> 21:51.768
your life in general
as a person who creates art for a living.

21:51.852 --> 21:53.478
Or maybe your goals
and plans for the future.

21:54.646 --> 21:55.772
[Ung breathes in sharply]

21:55.856 --> 21:56.857
I don't really have any.

21:58.233 --> 22:00.527
Can we just
skip to the next question, please?

22:00.610 --> 22:02.362
All right, then. Uh…

22:02.446 --> 22:05.324
Tell me how you began drawing.
Like, what moment got you into it?

22:12.831 --> 22:13.915
There's no story to tell.

22:13.999 --> 22:15.375
[dopey music]

22:15.959 --> 22:17.502
Okay, fine. You can say that then.

22:17.586 --> 22:20.213
Hold on. That's gonna
make him seem like a simpleton.

22:20.297 --> 22:21.256
Doesn't matter, it's the truth.

22:21.757 --> 22:23.425
No sugarcoating. Be true to yourself.

22:24.593 --> 22:25.719
[Ji-ung] Here we go.

22:29.639 --> 22:32.309
[Eun-ho sighing]
We're almost there now.

22:32.893 --> 22:33.769
Aren't you nervous?

22:34.936 --> 22:36.980
- Hmm?
- In a way, this is kinda like your debut.

22:37.064 --> 22:39.066
Your big introduction. Ta-da!

22:39.149 --> 22:41.985
Your very first public appearance. Crazy.
Aren't you nervous?

22:42.069 --> 22:43.862
If I say yes, are you gonna cancel it?

22:43.945 --> 22:45.489
No way in hell. Hang in there, dude.

22:46.239 --> 22:49.117
Oh, okay. I got just the song
for situations like this.

22:49.201 --> 22:52.245
- [beeping]
- Play "Island" by NJ, please.

22:53.789 --> 22:55.123
[song starts playing]

22:55.207 --> 22:58.668
Oh, God, I'm so glad.
You're finally out of your cave.

22:59.252 --> 23:00.462
I was never in a cave, dumbass.

23:01.046 --> 23:02.923
You actually were. Don't deny it.

23:04.591 --> 23:07.677
To be honest, I was worried sick
that you'd have trouble sleeping,

23:07.761 --> 23:09.596
and you'd become even more
depressed and anxious

23:09.679 --> 23:11.932
ever since Yeon-su
came back into your life.

23:12.015 --> 23:14.726
But no need to mull over it.
In the end, this is all thanks to her.

23:14.810 --> 23:16.478
Future's looking even brighter now.

23:16.561 --> 23:18.772
You would have never done this
if I came up with it.

23:18.855 --> 23:19.773
[Ung exhales]

23:19.856 --> 23:21.900
Anyway, I hope you'll enjoy doing this

23:21.983 --> 23:24.778
and maybe even continue
working with others out in the open.

23:25.779 --> 23:28.365
Then you'll become
even more famous, get a lot more work,

23:28.448 --> 23:30.200
and rake in all the moolah.

23:31.993 --> 23:33.578
That being said, what's your take

23:33.662 --> 23:36.414
on giving your outstanding manager
a raise after this?

23:36.498 --> 23:37.707
I'm passionately against it.

23:37.791 --> 23:39.876
Hmm. I see. Then let's take our time

23:39.960 --> 23:42.170
and discuss that topic more
sometime down the road.

23:42.254 --> 23:44.047
- What?
- And here we are.

23:45.924 --> 23:47.467
[cheery pop music]

23:48.927 --> 23:50.720
Go and head up to the second floor first.

23:50.804 --> 23:52.097
Your green room will be there.

23:52.180 --> 23:53.890
I'll go look for parking,
and I'll bring your stuff over.

23:53.974 --> 23:56.601
You can forget about the raise.
You already have your welfare--

23:56.685 --> 23:59.521
Oh, boy, we're holding back the road.
Go on, they're getting angry back there.

23:59.604 --> 24:00.438
[Ung grunts]

24:00.522 --> 24:02.399
- See you later.
- All right, I'll see you soon.

24:03.817 --> 24:06.069
[cheery pop music]

24:26.381 --> 24:28.884
LIVE DRAWING SHOW

24:28.967 --> 24:32.095
LIVE DRAWING SHOW

24:35.307 --> 24:37.559
GO-OH, NU-A
SEON SHOP OPENING DRAWING SHOW

24:49.738 --> 24:52.657
GO-OH

25:00.999 --> 25:03.293
[Ye-in] We should run it
by Ms. Kook before we do it.

25:03.960 --> 25:06.379
Mr. Kang, have you seen Ms. Kook?

25:06.463 --> 25:08.048
[Ji-un] I saw her heading
to the second floor.

25:08.131 --> 25:10.300
- [Ye-in] I see. Let's check the showroom.
- [Ji-un] Okay.

25:23.563 --> 25:26.733
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

25:49.005 --> 25:49.839
[chuckles softly]

25:49.923 --> 25:52.342
[Ung] She always looked
perpetually mad whenever we're together.

25:57.514 --> 25:58.515
I think…

25:59.891 --> 26:02.435
I finally appreciate Yeon-su
for who she is.

26:04.104 --> 26:05.772
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

26:15.991 --> 26:19.119
We already interviewed Ung this morning.
We just need Yeon-su's now.

26:19.202 --> 26:21.079
You don't need much,
just get some rough footage.

26:21.162 --> 26:23.456
Once the show begins,
make sure to focus on him.

26:23.540 --> 26:25.625
Intern, I want you to stay with her.

26:25.709 --> 26:27.252
Sure, you can count on that, sir.

26:27.335 --> 26:29.546
Should I interview her
before the event starts?

26:30.422 --> 26:31.506
No, I'll do it.

26:31.589 --> 26:33.675
We have a meeting
back at the office later,

26:33.758 --> 26:36.136
- so let's pick up the pace.
- [Chae-ran] Understood, sir.

26:37.304 --> 26:39.806
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim continues]

26:50.358 --> 26:51.818
[clears throat]

26:53.236 --> 26:56.531
- Oh.
- I'm sorry, is this the waiting area?

26:57.574 --> 26:59.075
[Yeon-su] What the… It's Ung.

26:59.784 --> 27:00.994
When did he even get here?

27:07.792 --> 27:08.626
[exhales]

27:17.427 --> 27:19.095
Great. What should I say?

27:19.679 --> 27:21.598
Do I wanna mention last night?

27:21.681 --> 27:22.849
About yesterday…

27:26.561 --> 27:27.937
You were at my place, right?

27:29.481 --> 27:30.690
[Yeon-su] I knew it.

27:31.524 --> 27:33.109
He doesn't remember at all.

27:35.653 --> 27:39.491
Yes. I had something to give you
so I went to your place.

27:40.283 --> 27:41.201
Hmm.

27:41.993 --> 27:43.370
[Ung clears throat]

27:43.870 --> 27:45.330
Then did I do something--

27:45.413 --> 27:47.624
- [phone buzzing]
- Oh, sorry.

27:47.707 --> 27:49.292
I need to get ready for the event.

27:49.376 --> 27:51.461
The staff will tell you the details
regarding the live show

27:51.544 --> 27:53.296
and everything else you need.

27:58.218 --> 28:02.222
[Yeon-su] But seriously, there's no reason
for me to be avoiding him like this.

28:03.348 --> 28:04.265
Hey.

28:06.518 --> 28:07.352
Good luck.

28:08.561 --> 28:09.437
Hmm.

28:11.898 --> 28:13.316
[gentle music]

28:14.359 --> 28:15.318
[door closes]

28:20.532 --> 28:21.533
[Eun-ho sighs]

28:22.283 --> 28:24.744
Oh, that's weird, you didn't run away.

28:24.828 --> 28:26.996
[Eun-ho] Take a rest, it's okay.
We'll just rehearse later.

28:27.080 --> 28:28.456
Here's the layout and program.

28:35.922 --> 28:37.340
LIVE DRAWING SHOW
GO-OH

28:38.550 --> 28:41.094
- Ms. Kook.
- Did you check Go-oh's video?

28:41.177 --> 28:43.096
Yes, I did. Everything's fine.
I checked the whole thing just now.

28:43.179 --> 28:45.724
Then go ahead and play it now, please,
alongside the playlist he's given us

28:45.807 --> 28:47.142
- and put it on a loop.
- Yep.

28:57.402 --> 28:59.446
["Christmas Tree" by V playing]

29:21.843 --> 29:23.094
[Yeon-su] Unbelievable.

29:24.137 --> 29:26.097
I've never seen that side of him before.

29:29.267 --> 29:30.435
[Ye-in] Ms. Kook.

29:31.352 --> 29:32.562
Ms. Kook.

29:36.858 --> 29:37.859
Ms. Kook.

29:46.868 --> 29:48.328
[Eun-ho] Ung, we need to head out.

29:50.622 --> 29:51.664
Are you asleep?

29:54.209 --> 29:56.669
You feeling a little tense?
Do you want some more Xanax?

29:57.378 --> 29:58.379
Why…

30:00.340 --> 30:01.883
Why did I sleep well last night?

30:02.884 --> 30:05.720
You say that like it's a problem.
Are you still hung up on that?

30:05.804 --> 30:07.472
[Eun-ho] Yo, can you
write a caption for this?

30:07.555 --> 30:09.682
Can you write,
"Pondering about what to draw"?

30:09.766 --> 30:11.100
Make him look all mysterious.

30:11.684 --> 30:13.019
[Ho] I think we can get a good view.

30:13.645 --> 30:15.271
Is this his? Which one?

30:15.355 --> 30:17.273
- No. It's the other one.
- This? Okay.

30:17.357 --> 30:18.483
[Yeon-ok] Come on, let's go.

30:20.777 --> 30:22.403
[guests chatting]

30:29.202 --> 30:31.287
- I won't see anything from here.
- Just sit down.

30:32.539 --> 30:34.374
- Come on.
- Let's sit at the front, right there.

30:35.750 --> 30:36.668
Nu-a is here.

30:37.418 --> 30:39.546
- [applause]
- [cheering]

30:42.048 --> 30:43.424
Hello. It's nice to meet you all.

30:44.092 --> 30:46.177
I'm honored to be able
to draw the buildings

30:46.261 --> 30:49.722
designed by my role model, Jean Ferrat,
more so in a setting such as this.

30:49.806 --> 30:51.224
I'm sure you're all aware,

30:51.307 --> 30:54.143
that another artist will be drawing
on the other side in parallel with me.

30:54.227 --> 30:56.938
- So if you're curious, go ahead and peek.
- [crowd laughing]

30:57.021 --> 30:59.607
[Nu-a] However, since you're already here,
I doubt any of you will.

30:59.691 --> 31:01.317
I guarantee you'll be
too immersed to move.

31:01.401 --> 31:04.612
I'll be doing my absolute best
to win your hearts as an illustrator.

31:04.696 --> 31:07.699
So now, ladies and gentlemen, I'm Nu-a.

31:07.782 --> 31:09.492
[applause]

31:12.745 --> 31:13.830
- Hey, son!
- [gasps]

31:14.664 --> 31:16.457
[whispers from audience]

31:19.085 --> 31:20.503
[Ho] That's my son.

31:21.212 --> 31:23.798
- [man 1] He's so good.
- [man 2] Didn't think he'd be this tall.

31:28.761 --> 31:30.763
["Christmas Tree" by V playing]

31:34.767 --> 31:38.313
♪ In this moment ♪

31:38.396 --> 31:41.232
♪ I see you ♪

31:41.900 --> 31:46.446
♪ It always comes around as I believed ♪

31:48.448 --> 31:51.993
♪ When the rain stops ♪

31:52.076 --> 31:54.996
♪ You shine on me ♪

31:55.496 --> 32:01.002
♪ Your light's the only thing
That keeps the cold out ♪

32:01.836 --> 32:05.214
♪ Moon in the summer night ♪

32:05.298 --> 32:08.384
♪ Whispering of the stars ♪

32:08.468 --> 32:09.969
♪ They're singing like ♪

32:10.053 --> 32:14.515
♪ Christmas trees for us ♪

32:15.725 --> 32:18.061
♪ So I'll tell you ♪

32:18.144 --> 32:21.648
♪ A million tiny things that ♪

32:21.731 --> 32:25.401
♪ You have never known ♪

32:25.485 --> 32:28.905
♪ It all gets tangled up inside ♪

32:29.489 --> 32:31.449
♪ And I'll tell you ♪

32:32.033 --> 32:35.411
♪ A million little reasons ♪

32:35.495 --> 32:39.123
♪ I'm falling for your eyes ♪

32:39.207 --> 32:43.920
♪ I just want to be where you are ♪

32:44.003 --> 32:45.588
♪ Tell you ♪

32:45.672 --> 32:48.967
♪ A million tiny things that ♪

32:49.050 --> 32:52.345
♪ You have never known ♪

32:52.845 --> 32:57.684
♪ It all gets tangled up inside ♪

32:57.767 --> 32:59.018
♪ Tell you ♪

32:59.602 --> 33:02.855
♪ A million little reasons ♪

33:02.939 --> 33:05.942
♪ I'm falling for your eyes ♪

33:06.025 --> 33:07.193
[Ji-ung] First time, huh?

33:07.276 --> 33:10.863
- ♪ I just want to be where you are ♪
- Uh-huh.

33:10.947 --> 33:12.907
I didn't know there was this side to him.

33:12.991 --> 33:14.784
[chuckles softly]
He's like a different guy.

33:14.867 --> 33:16.244
[Ji-ung chuckles]
Same here.

33:16.327 --> 33:19.580
He looked like a total stranger
the first time I saw him drawing.

33:19.664 --> 33:20.707
You're right.

33:22.291 --> 33:23.710
By the way, good job.

33:23.793 --> 33:27.380
This is quite a large-scale operation.
Must've been a pain to prepare this.

33:27.463 --> 33:29.090
No, really. All part of the work.

33:29.757 --> 33:32.635
Shouldn't you be working somewhere
instead of chatting with me?

33:32.719 --> 33:35.638
Exactly. I'm here to pick you up, Yeon-su.

33:38.141 --> 33:40.184
You can never judge a book by its cover.

33:40.268 --> 33:43.980
Who knew I'd be working side by side
with the lowest scoring kid?

33:44.564 --> 33:46.941
Obviously, he was
a nuisance all throughout.

33:47.025 --> 33:50.945
As you all know, we're incompatible.
He and I are strikingly different.

33:51.029 --> 33:52.780
Of course,
he's the annoying and frustrating type.

33:52.864 --> 33:55.450
During this project, he should've
shared his progress with me,

33:55.533 --> 33:57.618
so we'd be up to speed
to make things more efficient.

33:57.702 --> 33:59.454
But he never said a single word.

33:59.537 --> 34:00.830
Always just thinking to himself.

34:01.414 --> 34:02.874
He was always like that
from the beginning.

34:02.957 --> 34:05.084
I'd ask what was on his mind and it's,
"I don't know. Not sure.

34:05.168 --> 34:06.002
There's nothing to say."

34:06.085 --> 34:07.295
Either one of those.

34:08.379 --> 34:10.381
Great, I'm getting annoyed all over again.

34:10.465 --> 34:11.758
ANYTHING POSITIVE TO SAY ABOUT HIM?

34:11.841 --> 34:12.717
Nothing at all.

34:13.509 --> 34:14.510
Well…

34:14.594 --> 34:16.054
NOT EVEN ONE?

34:16.137 --> 34:19.182
I guess seeing him draw like that
for the first time kind of…

34:19.265 --> 34:22.435
it was like discovering
a new side of him I never noticed before.

34:23.603 --> 34:25.980
I mean, yes,
he used to draw a lot back then,

34:26.064 --> 34:28.733
but he never had
that serious look on his face before.

34:29.692 --> 34:32.570
I don't know what's gotten into him,
but he's completely focused,

34:32.653 --> 34:33.863
like he's in his element.

34:33.946 --> 34:35.698
Very different from the guy I know.

34:36.991 --> 34:38.284
But you know what?

34:38.367 --> 34:41.037
He was always serious about drawing,
it was his passion.

34:41.120 --> 34:43.247
If you check back,
I think it was in episode five,

34:43.331 --> 34:45.333
I accidentally ruined his drawing once,

34:45.416 --> 34:48.252
and he threw
a massive fit for days, like I hurt him.

34:48.336 --> 34:51.297
Honestly, I really did
feel bad about it. I did.

34:51.380 --> 34:54.258
But seeing him
all worked up was kind of entertaining.

34:54.842 --> 34:58.179
I mean, he rarely gets mad, you know.
He's always so quiet.

34:58.262 --> 34:59.597
I admit that I did tease him

34:59.680 --> 35:01.891
a few more times
to get a reaction for fun.

35:03.851 --> 35:04.811
[chuckles]

35:05.520 --> 35:07.396
He always made me laugh either way.

35:08.606 --> 35:10.525
["Drawer" by 10cm playing]

35:15.571 --> 35:16.656
Uhm…

35:17.490 --> 35:20.076
Yeah, basically
I'm not used to this side of him.

35:21.410 --> 35:24.622
I guess, it feels like he's changed.

35:27.166 --> 35:29.127
Funny, I thought he'd never change.

35:35.049 --> 35:38.386
Uhm, sorry, I was just rambling, wasn't I?
Let's cut that.

35:39.512 --> 35:41.806
- Okay, next question.
- Hmm.

35:43.766 --> 35:46.102
["Drawer" by 10cm continues]

36:03.327 --> 36:06.664
Huh. Shouldn't he
take a breather or something?

36:06.747 --> 36:09.584
Nah, this is how he always works.
All in till the end.

36:09.667 --> 36:13.004
But since there's an audience,
he probably feels even more tense.

36:14.547 --> 36:16.174
Good point. Let me go check up on him.

36:18.676 --> 36:21.220
- Honey, let's go.
- All right.

36:28.686 --> 36:31.981
Oh, wow. Is that you, Yeon-su?

36:32.064 --> 36:33.691
Hello, glad you're here.

36:33.774 --> 36:35.693
It's been ages since we saw each other.

36:35.776 --> 36:37.862
I heard you were
part of this project from the others.

36:37.945 --> 36:40.323
Yes. So how have you been lately?

36:40.406 --> 36:43.492
It's always the same for us.
Nothing's really changed.

36:43.576 --> 36:47.496
Goodness gracious. It's like
you haven't changed at all since then.

36:47.580 --> 36:49.165
Same goes for the both of you.

36:49.248 --> 36:51.083
Is it because of what we're wearing?

36:51.167 --> 36:53.377
Are you here to watch Ung's drawing show?

36:53.461 --> 36:54.712
Oh, yes, yes, yes.

36:54.795 --> 36:56.714
Then how come you're leaving already?

36:56.797 --> 36:59.342
Oh. It's kind of dragging, right?

36:59.425 --> 37:00.676
- No.
- [Yeon-ok] That's not why.

37:01.385 --> 37:04.847
[Yeon-ok] Seeing him draw all alone
like that, makes us feel uncomfortable.

37:04.931 --> 37:06.807
It reminds me
of the time when he was young.

37:07.516 --> 37:09.936
To think even back then
it was so normal for him--

37:10.019 --> 37:12.188
- [Ho] We should get going, come on.
- Okay.

37:12.271 --> 37:14.482
Hey, Yeon-su,
come over for a meal sometime.

37:14.565 --> 37:16.400
- You know you're always welcome.
- Okay.

37:16.484 --> 37:18.819
No need to think about it too much,
just come on over.

37:18.903 --> 37:20.947
Don't worry, it's free of charge.

37:21.447 --> 37:22.865
He's right. You should come visit us.

37:22.949 --> 37:24.408
I'll make you something good.

37:24.492 --> 37:26.577
- Come, come.
- I'll be seeing you, okay?

37:27.787 --> 37:28.663
[Yeon-ok chuckles]

37:39.423 --> 37:40.633
It's just that…

37:41.884 --> 37:44.011
the break-up devastated Ung.

37:45.429 --> 37:47.223
It must have been hard for you too.

37:47.306 --> 37:49.225
[gentle music]

37:54.146 --> 37:58.526
We really want you to visit us.
So please, come and drop by, okay?

37:58.609 --> 38:00.278
Okay. I will.

38:00.361 --> 38:01.862
All right. Goodbye.

38:02.446 --> 38:03.281
Mm-hmm.

38:04.115 --> 38:06.200
Come on. We have to go, Yeon-su.

38:06.284 --> 38:07.159
- Okay, okay.
- Hurry up.

38:07.243 --> 38:08.869
- Goodbye.
- Stop dragging your feet.

38:08.953 --> 38:10.413
Bye.

38:10.997 --> 38:12.915
[gentle music]

38:16.419 --> 38:17.712
[sighs]

38:30.725 --> 38:32.852
[gentle music continues]

38:48.576 --> 38:49.702
- Ji-ung.
- Hm?

38:50.369 --> 38:51.829
Did you do the interview with Yeon-su?

38:51.912 --> 38:53.789
Yeah. And the shoot?

38:54.457 --> 38:56.083
There's nothing to film, so…

38:56.167 --> 38:58.544
Not like we'll get much,
he's been sitting down for hours.

38:58.627 --> 39:01.589
Go back to the office with Tae-hun,
start preparing for the meeting.

39:01.672 --> 39:03.799
Don't wait for me.
I'll wrap things up over here.

39:08.846 --> 39:11.974
[Yeon-ok] It's just that
the break-up devastated Ung.

39:13.017 --> 39:14.560
[deep exhale]

39:14.643 --> 39:16.437
["Maybe If" by BIBI playing]

39:19.065 --> 39:20.274
[Ung] Wanna sleep over?

39:27.531 --> 39:29.992
Are you sick? Do you have a fever?

39:46.425 --> 39:48.594
[Yeon-su] How many pills
did you take anyway?

39:49.345 --> 39:50.805
Do you take them often?

39:50.888 --> 39:53.182
Huh? When did you start taking them?

39:53.265 --> 39:56.685
Since when did you have trouble sleeping?
Why didn't you tell me much sooner?

40:03.067 --> 40:04.026
[Yeon-su gasps softly]

40:06.654 --> 40:08.656
["Maybe If" by BIBI continues]

40:27.091 --> 40:28.050
[knocking]

40:29.093 --> 40:30.094
Yes?

40:31.345 --> 40:33.055
[Ye-in] Oh, someone told me
that you were here.

40:33.139 --> 40:35.433
Everything's going well. In fact,
Nu-a's finishing up his piece now.

40:35.516 --> 40:37.226
Uh, escort him to the first floor.

40:37.309 --> 40:40.020
Get him all set up and prepped
for the press conference when he's done.

40:40.104 --> 40:41.689
Stay with him there.
I'll escort Go-oh myself.

40:41.772 --> 40:43.190
Got it, Ms. Kook.

40:58.247 --> 40:59.498
[deep breath]

41:00.207 --> 41:01.959
[Ung] I still have a bit of time left.

41:02.543 --> 41:03.752
[surprised whispering]

41:04.336 --> 41:05.671
Hello, everyone.

41:05.754 --> 41:07.131
My name is Go-oh.

41:07.715 --> 41:10.092
- [applause]
- [loud cheering]

41:10.634 --> 41:13.262
[audience cheering]

41:33.574 --> 41:34.658
Oh…

41:34.742 --> 41:36.243
Hey, you. Congratulations.

41:38.496 --> 41:39.830
You look a little different today.

41:40.623 --> 41:41.665
[awkward chuckle]

41:43.584 --> 41:44.793
[reporter] Wow, it's NJ!

41:44.877 --> 41:47.421
[audience talking excitedly]

41:47.505 --> 41:49.089
[cameras clicking rapidly]

41:51.050 --> 41:53.302
[reporters clamoring]

41:57.223 --> 41:58.432
[slow somber music]

41:58.933 --> 42:01.227
[reporters continue clamoring]

42:02.186 --> 42:03.938
- [reporter] NJ.
- [cameras continue clicking]

42:04.730 --> 42:06.398
[slow somber music]

42:23.374 --> 42:25.084
GO-OH, NU-A
SOEN SHOP OPENING DRAWING SHOW

42:25.668 --> 42:26.669
How's it going, Ms. Kook?

42:26.752 --> 42:28.462
How's everything?
It must have been a long day.

42:28.546 --> 42:30.422
Thank you so much for your work today.

42:30.506 --> 42:33.717
There's an after-party later, so feel free
to come, you're all invited to attend.

42:33.801 --> 42:36.345
Uh, I'll just wrap things up over here.
You can all go.

42:36.929 --> 42:39.348
Are you sure?
We can help you wrap up, we don't mind.

42:39.431 --> 42:42.685
It's okay. You had to work on the weekend.
You deserve to relax. Thank you. Go.

42:42.768 --> 42:44.687
Are you also coming to the after-party?

42:44.770 --> 42:46.897
I don't know yet. We'll see. Go ahead.

42:46.981 --> 42:48.691
All right, you have a good day, then.

42:48.774 --> 42:51.485
- Hope to see you later.
- You have to come, you deserve it too.

42:59.285 --> 43:00.536
[groans]

43:01.161 --> 43:03.831
[somber music]

43:09.211 --> 43:10.045
[sighs]

43:13.382 --> 43:16.176
Why the hell
isn't that jackass picking up his phone?

43:17.303 --> 43:18.429
Ung, over here! Come.

43:18.512 --> 43:20.055
[Ung] Hey, why weren't you picking up?

43:20.139 --> 43:22.516
Hey, stranger.
All done with the press conference?

43:22.600 --> 43:24.143
NJ! What are you still doing here?

43:24.226 --> 43:26.729
Oh, I guess you're not excited to see me.

43:26.812 --> 43:29.356
Watch what you say next time,
you ungrateful fool.

43:29.440 --> 43:31.233
She personally made time
to see you all the way out here.

43:31.317 --> 43:33.485
Uh. Thank you so much
for coming to watch me.

43:33.569 --> 43:35.237
I didn't expect you to come here.

43:35.321 --> 43:36.905
I didn't think I'd come
uninvited to an event,

43:36.989 --> 43:38.407
just to see someone either.

43:38.490 --> 43:41.368
I actually arrived late
'cause of my schedule, but I still came.

43:41.452 --> 43:43.078
Gotta say, you looked different out there.

43:43.162 --> 43:45.164
NJ, I'll make extra sure
to send you an invite next time.

43:46.498 --> 43:49.418
Oh, right. Just a heads up,
in case you get all flustered

43:49.501 --> 43:51.920
seeing your name in
the top trending list in a few minutes,

43:52.004 --> 43:53.589
I told the reporters it's nothing weird.

43:53.672 --> 43:55.633
We're just two good friends
rooting for each other,

43:55.716 --> 43:56.925
so don't worry about anything.

43:57.509 --> 43:59.595
- Good friends?
- Well, yeah. Aren't we?

44:00.179 --> 44:01.472
Well, we… no, I…

44:01.555 --> 44:02.598
Yeah, of course we are.

44:03.390 --> 44:05.643
I'm just kinda flattered
you consider me as a friend.

44:06.894 --> 44:07.978
You're the first guy ever

44:08.062 --> 44:10.105
- who's happy to be friend-zoned by me.
- What?

44:10.189 --> 44:12.191
[gasps]
Never mind.

44:12.941 --> 44:14.443
Are you going home? Do you need a ride?

44:14.526 --> 44:16.070
It's okay.
We drove here as well. We'll be fine.

44:16.153 --> 44:17.488
Okay. You take care now.

44:17.571 --> 44:18.822
Sorry? Hold on.

44:18.906 --> 44:20.366
Is that the only reason
you were waiting for me?

44:20.449 --> 44:23.661
I already told you.
I'm very busy, but also I'm not.

44:23.744 --> 44:25.371
- Take care.
- Have a safe trip.

44:28.999 --> 44:30.417
Take care of yourself!

44:33.879 --> 44:36.382
Hey, Ung, how could you
decline her offer? What are you nuts?

44:36.465 --> 44:37.925
I'm exhausted. Shut up.

44:38.509 --> 44:41.345
- Anyway, this is pretty huge.
- What is?

44:41.428 --> 44:44.306
Today, you finally revealed yourself
to the adoring public,

44:44.390 --> 44:46.475
not to mention
instantly winning everyone's hearts.

44:46.558 --> 44:48.310
Bullshit. Just go and get the car, please.

44:48.894 --> 44:51.772
So by extension, this pretty much means
that you've agreed to give me a big raise.

44:51.855 --> 44:53.899
Shut up. I said, go and get the car.

44:55.567 --> 44:56.944
This was from NJ, right?

44:58.362 --> 45:00.572
- Oh, my God, it smells different.
- [both chuckle]

45:02.282 --> 45:04.701
Go-oh has finally debuted!

45:05.452 --> 45:06.328
[cheers]

45:10.749 --> 45:12.835
[soft music]

45:17.798 --> 45:18.674
[exhales]

45:19.299 --> 45:20.259
That's sweet.

45:21.635 --> 45:22.803
God, you're so pathetic.

45:23.637 --> 45:26.765
Can't believe you're here to pity party
on such a freaking great day.

45:26.849 --> 45:29.435
What are you talking about?
I came in case you were bored.

45:30.436 --> 45:33.856
You got the bad juju.
Probably why this place is failing.

45:33.939 --> 45:35.232
You should be at that party

45:35.315 --> 45:37.901
celebrating the fact
that the project was a success!

45:37.985 --> 45:40.863
You actually passed with flying colors,
but instead, you're here sulking.

45:40.946 --> 45:42.948
- I like this more.
- This is beyond being pathetic.

45:43.031 --> 45:45.826
Aren't you ecstatic all that hard work
you've been doing paid off?

45:46.994 --> 45:49.830
Uh, not really. It's all just work.

45:49.913 --> 45:52.499
Now that we're done,
it's on to the next project.

45:55.252 --> 45:56.587
Things really tough at work?

45:57.254 --> 46:00.299
No. It's actually easier
compared to my old job.

46:01.049 --> 46:03.427
Yeah, I guess it's pretty good.

46:05.929 --> 46:07.139
Then what's the problem?

46:11.977 --> 46:14.313
It's not demanding enough to challenge me,

46:15.522 --> 46:16.899
not exactly fun either.

46:18.984 --> 46:21.653
- That's all. Pretty much.
- [glass clanks]

46:21.737 --> 46:22.654
[clicks tongue]

46:24.615 --> 46:25.782
Have another.

46:35.918 --> 46:37.294
Remember what you said?

46:38.170 --> 46:40.756
You said that my eyes
looked empty and soulless.

46:40.839 --> 46:42.132
There was nothing in them.

46:43.217 --> 46:44.760
Hmm. They're still the same.

46:44.843 --> 46:48.347
So empty that the fish I've got back there
have livelier eyes than you.

46:49.932 --> 46:54.686
Well, I saw this look in Ung's eyes
as he was drawing today.

46:56.355 --> 46:59.399
They seemed so animated.
Like they were so full of life.

47:02.236 --> 47:03.362
Really?

47:03.862 --> 47:04.863
Hmm.

47:05.948 --> 47:09.243
He was so focused on his drawing,
you could feel all his passion.

47:11.119 --> 47:12.579
To be honest, I was jealous.

47:12.663 --> 47:13.705
[scoffs]

47:13.789 --> 47:15.832
What exactly would you be jealous of?

47:15.916 --> 47:17.084
[chuckles softly]

47:17.167 --> 47:19.378
Do I sound pathetic?
[chuckles]

47:19.461 --> 47:21.672
I always hated people
that I thought were pathetic.

47:22.756 --> 47:24.883
While he was working on improving himself,

47:25.384 --> 47:27.219
there I was, stagnant

47:27.302 --> 47:30.389
and busy making ends meet
with the soulless eyes of mine.

47:30.973 --> 47:33.308
Yup. Even I would think I'm pathetic.

47:33.976 --> 47:35.477
Christ. You're ridiculous.

47:36.228 --> 47:38.313
You weren't stagnating,
let alone being soulless.

47:38.397 --> 47:39.856
Think of the debt you had to pay off.

47:39.940 --> 47:42.109
Now that was tough,
I saw how hard you worked.

47:42.609 --> 47:43.569
Those are wins in life.

47:43.652 --> 47:45.988
And you've succeeded
by coming this far, you fool.

47:47.281 --> 47:48.240
[chuckles softly]

47:48.991 --> 47:51.285
Tonight I'm going to celebrate
a successful project.

47:51.368 --> 47:53.996
So consider me as your VIP.
Line up the soju bottles.

47:54.079 --> 47:56.707
- Okay, I already put nine on your tab.
- Really?

47:56.790 --> 47:59.001
Don't worry,
I'll be ripping you off all night.

47:59.918 --> 48:02.963
- Oh. Good evening.
- [man] Hello, good evening.

48:03.964 --> 48:05.048
- [woman] Where?
- [man] Over here?

48:05.132 --> 48:06.425
- [Sol-i] Thank you.
- [woman] Okay.

48:06.967 --> 48:08.135
[sighs]

48:09.511 --> 48:11.513
[soft gentle music]

48:12.639 --> 48:14.641
- [Sol-i] Here's the menu.
- [man] What's today's special?

48:14.725 --> 48:17.019
- [Sol-i] Today, it's jjamppong rice.
- [woman] I'll have the bibimpap. No wait…

48:17.644 --> 48:18.979
[groans]

48:19.062 --> 48:20.939
Hey, Ung, good work today.

48:22.816 --> 48:25.027
I'm going home. You get some good rest.

48:25.527 --> 48:26.445
Hmm.

48:27.321 --> 48:30.616
Hey. On your way out,
can you turn off that light?

48:30.699 --> 48:32.868
All right. See ya.

48:32.951 --> 48:34.036
Hmm.

48:36.038 --> 48:37.331
[Ung groans]

48:38.415 --> 48:39.541
[switch clicks]

48:39.625 --> 48:40.709
[sighs]

48:42.628 --> 48:44.004
[groans softly]

48:46.423 --> 48:47.507
[phone buzzing]

48:51.011 --> 48:52.638
[soft music]

48:54.097 --> 48:56.558
- [indistinct chatter]
- [glasses clinking]

49:02.439 --> 49:03.690
[Sol-i] And here's your order.

49:04.483 --> 49:06.276
- I'll take the empty bottles.
- [man] Okay.

49:07.110 --> 49:09.696
Hey, you're here.
Sorry for calling out of the blue.

49:09.780 --> 49:12.366
I'm sure you know,
I'm pretty much the only friend she has.

49:12.449 --> 49:15.577
Unfortunately, I'm too busy tonight
I can't get rid of her myself.

49:15.661 --> 49:17.454
I can't hand her over
to the police either.

49:18.246 --> 49:21.375
She'll get mad when she wakes up.
Actually, who really cares.

49:21.458 --> 49:22.459
Take her.

49:23.293 --> 49:25.545
Yeah. One minute, please.

49:27.464 --> 49:29.341
[soft gentle music]

49:43.271 --> 49:44.106
That you, Ung?

49:57.953 --> 49:59.830
[gasps]
That's so cold.

50:03.792 --> 50:04.876
[Ji-ung] You awake yet?

50:05.877 --> 50:06.878
[groans in agreement]

50:10.882 --> 50:12.801
- [yawns loudly]
- Didn't get enough rest?

50:12.884 --> 50:13.760
Uh-huh.

50:15.387 --> 50:17.139
On top of that,
I may have drunk a little bit.

50:17.723 --> 50:19.725
- I'm a little drunk.
- Drink this.

50:19.808 --> 50:21.768
Oh, how considerate.

50:23.437 --> 50:24.646
[sips]

50:26.940 --> 50:27.774
[gulps]

50:29.234 --> 50:32.154
Sorry. What time is it?
Must have been a hassle.

50:32.237 --> 50:35.824
Not really.
I was at a boring get-together.

50:35.907 --> 50:38.034
- Did you drink too?
- A little bit.

50:38.118 --> 50:39.161
But you're a lightweight.

50:40.662 --> 50:42.873
- You remember that?
- [Yeon-su] Of course I do.

50:42.956 --> 50:45.167
Like watching a grown man
who couldn't handle baby sips.

50:45.250 --> 50:46.418
[scoffs]

50:46.501 --> 50:47.502
Okay, that's a stretch.

50:48.837 --> 50:49.755
[inhales]

50:55.635 --> 50:58.805
By the way,
how's the documentary going anyway?

50:58.889 --> 51:00.974
[breathes in sharply]
Well, it's going okay.

51:01.558 --> 51:04.144
I regret agreeing to do it again
after all these years.

51:04.770 --> 51:07.731
Back in high school, at least we were
young and cute, which was fine to watch.

51:07.814 --> 51:09.983
But now all they're gonna get
is a bunch of adults working.

51:10.066 --> 51:11.485
It'll just be boring.

51:11.568 --> 51:12.402
[clicks tongue]

51:12.486 --> 51:14.780
I'm afraid this whole thing
is gonna be a flop.

51:14.863 --> 51:16.239
Sounds like wishful thinking on your part.

51:16.323 --> 51:18.533
So? I'll make sure
no one ever gets to watch it.

51:18.617 --> 51:20.577
You know how I am at promoting things.

51:20.660 --> 51:24.539
- I'm going to spread a rumor.
- [chuckles]

51:25.957 --> 51:26.792
[sniffs]

51:27.417 --> 51:30.670
But if you agree to let me watch it first,
I might change my mind.

51:31.838 --> 51:34.508
- You wanna watch it?
- I may have looked ugly in some shots

51:34.591 --> 51:36.927
or blurted out
a swear word or two without realizing it.

51:37.010 --> 51:40.096
I'm pretty sure that Ung
was talking crap about me all throughout.

51:41.181 --> 51:44.184
Anyway, just curious. That's all.

51:49.397 --> 51:52.192
By the way, what did Ung say about me?

51:52.734 --> 51:53.735
Was it all bad?

52:01.201 --> 52:02.202
I mean…

52:03.203 --> 52:04.830
- [Yeon-su] Did he just shit-talk about--
- Hey…

52:07.624 --> 52:09.167
You still like him, don't you?

52:10.794 --> 52:12.963
[gentle music]

52:23.640 --> 52:26.560
[Ji-ung] Hey.
You still like him, don't you?

52:28.103 --> 52:29.646
[Yeon-su] No. That's impossible.

52:43.869 --> 52:45.662
There's no way this is happening.

52:45.745 --> 52:46.788
Choi Ung?

52:52.377 --> 52:54.087
What are you doing out here so late?

52:54.838 --> 52:57.924
I found out
that you moved back here recently.

52:59.467 --> 53:01.428
I guess that's why
we kept running into each other.

53:02.012 --> 53:03.930
Oh, I guess.

53:06.349 --> 53:07.642
Did you have a drink?

53:08.226 --> 53:10.645
What? Uh…
[clears throat]

53:11.229 --> 53:12.397
Hmm.

53:13.356 --> 53:15.901
I did. Anyway, what are you
doing out here? It's kinda late.

53:17.527 --> 53:18.945
Yeah, I guess.

53:19.029 --> 53:21.281
It was already late
when I got here earlier,

53:21.364 --> 53:23.742
so I was debating
if maybe I should just go.

53:24.701 --> 53:25.535
Uh…

53:26.369 --> 53:29.164
If it's not that urgent,
maybe we can just talk next time?

53:29.247 --> 53:30.540
I'm really tired right now.

53:31.041 --> 53:31.958
[gasps]

53:36.630 --> 53:38.965
[soft gentle music]

54:28.640 --> 54:31.017
[light sweet music]

54:39.275 --> 54:40.652
Hey, it's you again.

54:46.116 --> 54:47.283
Am I dreaming?

54:56.001 --> 54:57.252
I won't fall for it.

55:03.049 --> 55:04.134
Yeon-su.

55:14.185 --> 55:15.770
I've been in so much pain.

55:29.951 --> 55:32.620
[Yeon-su] No, I remember all of it.

55:33.204 --> 55:35.832
You okay? You seem pretty wasted.

55:37.250 --> 55:38.835
No, I'm fine. I'm just tired.

55:42.589 --> 55:43.673
You…

55:45.425 --> 55:46.259
About last night…

55:48.887 --> 55:52.390
Well, I saw a Thermos bottle at my house.

55:52.474 --> 55:53.933
I was wondering if you left it there.

55:55.226 --> 55:58.021
[Yeon-su] Thank God.
I'm glad he doesn't remember anything.

55:59.731 --> 56:03.401
Yes. You kind of seemed like you were
out of it, so I just left it there.

56:05.111 --> 56:06.446
Oh, really?

56:06.529 --> 56:10.533
Mm-hmm. You were on some pills.
All dazed and stuff.

56:11.409 --> 56:13.495
Did I fall asleep right after you left?

56:14.788 --> 56:15.789
I think so.

56:18.583 --> 56:20.627
Oh, okay then.

56:21.544 --> 56:23.379
Did you come all the way here
to ask me that?

56:24.214 --> 56:25.590
[awkward chuckle]
You could've just called.

56:30.595 --> 56:32.680
Looks like
I'm the only one who'll remember.

56:33.932 --> 56:35.266
I should go inside now.

56:35.975 --> 56:37.102
See ya.

56:37.685 --> 56:39.813
Guess I'll just take it to my grave.

56:39.896 --> 56:43.274
[Ung] Tomorrow, you should
just pretend that you don't remember.

56:46.277 --> 56:47.445
It wasn't a dream.

56:52.200 --> 56:53.535
There's no need to lie.

56:58.331 --> 56:59.541
So why pretend?

57:01.626 --> 57:02.710
Yeon-su.

57:09.968 --> 57:10.969
Yeon-su.

57:11.636 --> 57:13.638
["There For You" by Kim Na Young playing]

57:28.111 --> 57:29.446
Do you think this is right?

57:33.241 --> 57:35.410
Do you think
what we're doing right now is right?

57:46.963 --> 57:49.382
We're not like everyone else. We're us.

57:53.178 --> 57:55.138
Our love for each other wasn't lukewarm…

57:58.683 --> 58:00.602
and in the same way,
neither was our breakup.

58:02.645 --> 58:04.314
It's been way too long.

58:06.149 --> 58:07.734
We should be able to…

58:08.318 --> 58:09.486
[soft sniffle]

58:10.528 --> 58:12.113
…ask each other "How have you been?"

58:13.573 --> 58:14.908
"How tough has it been for you?"

58:16.868 --> 58:19.621
"It's been tough for me."
We're allowed to say those things.

58:21.122 --> 58:22.207
[exhales deeply]

58:23.249 --> 58:24.834
[Yeon-su] The reason we broke up…

58:28.671 --> 58:29.756
How have you been?

58:30.632 --> 58:32.717
…it was because I was arrogant.

58:32.800 --> 58:34.052
Answer me.

58:35.845 --> 58:36.971
How have you been, Yeon-su?

58:38.056 --> 58:40.391
[Yeon-su] I was so arrogant,
I thought I could live…

58:42.602 --> 58:43.728
without you.

58:45.480 --> 58:47.273
["There For You"
by Kim Na Young continues]

58:57.116 --> 59:04.123
PRIDE AND PREJUDICE

59:25.895 --> 59:28.147
I'm going to keep that as a hobby.

59:28.231 --> 59:31.109
[Ung] What I want
is to bask in the sun during the day

59:31.192 --> 59:33.444
and lay underneath a lamp at night time.

59:33.528 --> 59:35.280
A stressful life just isn't for me.

59:36.155 --> 59:36.990
I'll be right back.

59:41.494 --> 59:43.496
[sighs]
I sounded pathetic didn't I?

59:48.501 --> 59:49.711
[sighs]

59:49.794 --> 59:53.131
JOBS FOR DESIGN MAJORS

59:55.717 --> 59:56.718
HOW EASY IS IT TO GET A JOB?

59:56.801 --> 59:58.595
MAKING MONEY THROUGH DRAWING

59:59.971 --> 01:00:02.890
4 MONTHS AFTER THE BREAKUP

01:00:05.143 --> 01:00:10.023
♪ It always comes around as I believed ♪

01:00:11.858 --> 01:00:15.278
♪ When the rain stops ♪

01:00:15.361 --> 01:00:18.740
♪ You shine on me ♪

01:00:18.823 --> 01:00:24.287
♪ Your light's the only thing
That keeps the cold out ♪

01:00:25.204 --> 01:00:28.416
♪ Moon in the summer night ♪

01:00:28.499 --> 01:00:31.502
♪ Whispering of the stars ♪

01:00:31.586 --> 01:00:33.296
♪ They're singing like ♪

01:00:33.379 --> 01:00:37.342
♪ Christmas trees for us ♪

01:00:38.926 --> 01:00:41.387
♪ So I'll tell you ♪

01:00:41.471 --> 01:00:44.849
♪ A million tiny things that ♪

01:00:44.932 --> 01:00:48.186
♪ You have never known ♪

01:00:48.686 --> 01:00:52.440
♪ It all gets tangled up inside ♪

01:00:52.523 --> 01:00:55.193
♪ And I'll tell you ♪

01:00:55.276 --> 01:00:57.570
♪ A million little reasons… ♪
